{"id":"G868","lema":"ἀφίστημι","lemaStrong":"ἀφίστημι","translit":"aphístēmi","pron":"","glosa":"","defStrong":"to remove, i.e. (actively) instigate to revolt; usually (reflexively) to desist, desert, etc.","defKjv":"depart, draw (fall) away, refrain, withdraw self","derivacion":"from G575 (ἀπό) and G2476 (ἵστημι);","veces":15,"versos":15,"refs":["Lc 2:37","Lc 4:13","Lc 8:13","Lc 13:27","Hch 5:37","Hch 5:38","Hch 12:10","Hch 15:38","Hch 19:9","Hch 22:29","2 Co 12:8","1 Ti 4:1","1 Ti 6:5","2 Ti 2:19","He 3:12"],"texto":"Textus Receptus (Scrivener 1894)"}